      "description": "Information plaque about a Neale's ball token instrument at the Railway Museum in Mysore, India. The plaque reads: Designed and manufactured initially at England this instrument is used to dispatch one train from one station to adjacent station. A token which is the tangible authority is extracted from this instrument by on duty station master in co-operation with the interconnected other end station master and handed over to the driver of the train to leave the station. No other train can be allowed to enter into the in-between these stations. A hand micro telephone is attached to this instrument for point to point communication with other end instrument.",
